    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the owner's date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts **1 July**, labelled by the calendar year in which it ends, e.g. a registration on/after 1 July 2026 is **FY27**).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** (`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`):\n- Added a `fiscalYear` mapping and a `fiscalYear(owner)` method returning `FY<YY>` derived from the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` (the stored `registrationDate` is already rolled to a business day by the create endpoint).\n- Added a private static `fiscalYearEnding(LocalDate)` helper (`month >= July ? year+1 : year`) used by all three derivations.\n- `membershipNumber` now uses the fiscal-year `YY` for its `-M<YY>` segment instead of the raw calendar year.\n- `hasQualifyingTenure` now counts **elapsed fiscal years** (`currentFY - registrationFY >= 1`) rather than a 365-day window. A newly created owner shares the current fiscal year, so it still earns zero tenure points \u2014 preserving the documented invariant.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`):\n- Added the read-only `fiscalYear` schema field (`FY<YY>`).\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nThe acceptance test's returned owner now carries `fiscalYear` matching `FY\\d{2}`, and the audit log confirms the identifier tracks the fiscal year (`membershipNumber=NSW-...-M27` for an 11 Aug 2026 registration).\n\nOne design decision worth flagging: the spec says `FY<YY>` without pinning the labelling convention. Given the app's Australian context I labelled the fiscal year by its **ending** year (ATO/corporate convention: FY27 = 1 Jul 2026\u201330 Jun 2027). The tenure threshold I read as \"at least one fiscal year has elapsed\" (crossed into a later fiscal year), the natural analogue of the old \"more than a year.\" If you intended the *starting* year as the label, or a stricter tenure threshold, those are one-line changes.",
